# Bytes, unchanged, on every platform.
#
# The corpus is vendored evidence: the reference implementation's verdicts were
# recorded against these exact files, and a gate hashes them to say they have
# not moved. Git's default is to rewrite line endings on checkout, so a Windows
# runner got a working tree where every XML file differed from its manifest —
# fifteen "changed" entries in a corpus nobody had touched.
#
# The same is true of the fixtures a generator writes, the SVGs the front page
# points at by hash, and the wheels a gate opens. This project decides what its
# files contain; the checkout does not get a vote.
* -text
